  "notes": "The straight-time, live-players end of this container, and it inverts almost every crunk default. `halfTime` is false and the backbeat goes to 2&4, the hats are continuous 8ths rather than a stopping 16th layer, the ghost snares come back at the parent's highest probability, and the harmony moves — i–iv–VII and i–VI–III–VII over slow 4-bar loops instead of a static i. ⛔ The load-bearing override is `drums.bass808.role`: N.O. Joe's account is \"real drums and I had a little 808 bottom to it but not as much\", and Scarface plays bass and guitar himself. The 808 is a floor, not the bassline, so the role is moved off `bassline` and the `bassline` block becomes a real played part — `independent_riff`, `followRootsProb` 0.6, a 20-semitone register, chord-tone passing notes. ⚠ `counter_riff` is the engine's only other role and it is a near-fit rather than a description: with `slideProb` at 0.03 the 808 stays on its root, which is what a floor does. The organ is `timbreHint`, because the research calls it \"a structural element\" rather than colour, and the arrangement's `fillBeforeSection` is false because the research says sections are \"marked by instrument entries rather than drum fills\". ⚠ `medium`, tracking the research's high-medium: the live-drums/organ/guitar method and his production role are sourced, the 76–94 BPM band is marked LOW-CONF and the perc lanes and chord weights are INFERRED. ⚠ `fills.snareRollLadder` is off — with both fill periods at 4 bars the big fill wins and the inherited ladder reads no seed, writing one identical fill on every one of them. ⚠ **`lockTo808` raised from 0.4 to 0.47.** The 808 takes each kick with this probability, and at 0.4 over this model's 12-kick floor a seed could produce no 808 at all — which `bass808.rs` refuses, because a declared 808 that sometimes vanishes is a part a producer cannot rely on. It is still well under a lock: a good share of kicks carry no sub. ⚠ The bass ceiling came down from 48 to 47 so it stays under a chord part that starts at 48 — `coherence.rs` requires the highest bass note to sit at or below the lowest chord note, and this model overlapped by 1.",
